    "The desktop product shell now starts a workspace-scoped loopback MCP runtime and a fresh Windows export replay produced a real listening endpoint plus a non-secret connection file. The current automation host cannot safely activate the one-time token control inside JCEF, so authenticated external-Agent replay on the selected installed candidate is still required before promotion.",
    "Release Git Tags contain SSH signatures; GitHub reports unknown_key until the public signing key is registered.",
    "Stage 11 full Java element support and the local 8-generator Gradle/JAR golden matrix pass; fixed-commit CI/Nightly and new candidate Windows install/upgrade/uninstall plus provenance evidence are still required before the next release candidate.",
    "The real JCEF accessibility pass and final clean Windows 11 RC replay are not complete; the Hyper-V guest cannot validate Chromium WebContents accessibility because native Edge reproduces the same missing web-control subtree, so a physical or otherwise known-good Windows accessibility environment is required.",
    "The current Beta scope explicitly excludes the real JCEF accessibility audit, final clean-Windows RC replay, and external tester trial; those exclusions are not claims that the omitted checks passed.",
